1. [MAJOR] src/cli.rs:147 — the new branch rejecting an inline value on a value-less flag (`--verbose=yes` for a default `yes/no` flag) is never exercised anywhere in `tests/module_system_test.rs:498-1107`; the report's matrix claims `--flag=value` coverage, but every inline test uses a value-taking flag or an explicit `takes_value: yes`. Add a test asserting `sys.parse([{name:"verbose", type:"yes/no"}], ["--verbose=yes"])` fails with "Flag '--verbose' does not take a value" on both engines, and decide explicitly whether `--verbose=false` should be accepted. (No behavior was observed broken; this is an untested error branch.)
2. [MINOR] tests/module_system_test.rs:428 — `cli_ran` compares the two engines' errors only by `label()` and `message()`; `cli_eval_err` (line 457) then returns the walked error, so the compiled engine's `Span` is never asserted. A VM error carrying an unknown span/line/column would pass every CLI test. Compare `walked_error.span()` with `compiled_error.span()`, or assert `is_known()` on both errors, in `cli_ran`/`cli_assert_runtime_error`.

